# Nanexus V0.1 — configuration template (no secrets)
#
# Two loading paths (do not confuse them):
#
# 1) Frigate private file (NANEXUS_FRIGATE_* only for the VMS client)
#    mkdir -p .local
#    cp .env.example .local/frigate.env
#    # edit .local/frigate.env — keep secrets out of Git (.local/ is gitignored)
#    The Web process reads that file via NANEXUS_FRIGATE_ENV (default
#    .local/frigate.env) and applies NANEXUS_FRIGATE_* keys to the Frigate client.
#
# 2) Web / Ollama process environment (NANEXUS_WEB_*, NANEXUS_OLLAMA_*, models, TZ)
#    These are read from the process environment by WebConfig — NOT from the
#    Frigate file alone. Either export them in the shell, or source a file into
#    the environment before starting nanexus-web, for example:
#      set -a
#      source .local/web.env   # optional file you create with WEB/OLLAMA keys only
#      set +a
#      uv run nanexus-web
#
# Copying .env.example to .local/frigate.env does NOT by itself activate
# NANEXUS_WEB_* or NANEXUS_OLLAMA_* settings.
#
# Never commit real passwords, tokens, private CA material, or personal IPs.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frigate connection (REQUIRED for live VMS investigations)
# Loaded from the Frigate env file (see NANEXUS_FRIGATE_ENV).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authenticated Frigate entry only (typically HTTPS on port 8971).
# Do not use the unauthenticated internal port (5000).
NANEXUS_FRIGATE_BASE_URL=https://frigate.example:8971

# Stable VMS instance id used in evidence locators (string of your choosing).
NANEXUS_FRIGATE_VMS_INSTANCE_ID=frigate-example

# Comma-separated camera names Nanexus is allowed to query (REQUIRED).
NANEXUS_FRIGATE_CAMERAS=front_yard

# Auth — provide exactly ONE method (restricted/viewer-class credentials recommended):
#   A) username + password, OR
#   B) bearer token, OR
#   C) session cookie.
# Do not put admin Frigate credentials here.
NANEXUS_FRIGATE_USERNAME=viewer
NANEXUS_FRIGATE_PASSWORD=replace-me
# NANEXUS_FRIGATE_BEARER_TOKEN=
# NANEXUS_FRIGATE_SESSION_COOKIE=

# HTTPS trust (REQUIRED when BASE_URL is https://)
# Path to a CA/trust bundle file that validates the Frigate certificate.
NANEXUS_FRIGATE_CA_BUNDLE=/path/to/frigate-ca-or-pinned-cert.pem

# Optional: disable TLS hostname verification (only for known SAN-less lab certs).
# Prefer a correct CA/SAN setup when possible.
# NANEXUS_FRIGATE_DISABLE_HOSTNAME_CHECK=1

# Optional: max events requested per Frigate list call (default 50).
# NANEXUS_FRIGATE_MAX_LIMIT=50

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web console — process environment (OPTIONAL; defaults are localhost-safe)
# Export these in the shell (or source a separate web.env). They are NOT applied
# merely by being present in .local/frigate.env.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Path to the Frigate env file that supplies NANEXUS_FRIGATE_* to the Web process.
# This is a process-environment setting (default shown). It is NOT read from inside
# the Frigate file itself.
# NANEXUS_FRIGATE_ENV=.local/frigate.env

# Bind address and port (default: 127.0.0.1:8787). Do not use 0.0.0.0 for V0.1.
# NANEXUS_WEB_HOST=127.0.0.1
# NANEXUS_WEB_PORT=8787

# Durable Case DB and retained-media root (created under .local/ by default).
# NANEXUS_WEB_DOMAIN_DB=.local/web/domain.sqlite
# NANEXUS_WEB_MEDIA_ROOT=.local/web/media_store

# live (default) or stub (deterministic tests only).
# NANEXUS_WEB_BACKEND=live
# NANEXUS_WEB_STUB_CAMERAS=front_yard

# Temporary LAN UI review only: comma-separated client IPs allowed to connect.
# This is NOT multi-user authentication. Leave unset for localhost-only.
# NANEXUS_WEB_ALLOWED_CLIENTS=

# Operator timezone label shown in the UI (inputs still use the browser clock).
# NANEXUS_TZ=America/Toronto

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local Ollama — process environment (OPTIONAL overrides)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NANEXUS_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# NANEXUS_CHAT_MODEL=qwen3:14b
# NANEXUS_VISUAL_MODEL=moondream:1.8b

# Set to 0/false/no to disable observe_media / local VLM even if the model exists.
# NANEXUS_ENABLE_OBSERVE=1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live pytest scope (OPTIONAL; required only for pytest -m live_frigate)
# Do not commit site-specific historical investigation windows.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NANEXUS_TEST_LIVE_START=2024-01-15T12:00:00+00:00
# NANEXUS_TEST_LIVE_END=2024-01-15T13:00:00+00:00
# NANEXUS_TEST_LIVE_TZ=UTC
